# Loading, Error & Async UX Patterns

## Every Route Must Have a `pendingComponent`

No blank screens during data loading. Create a skeleton component and wire it:

```typescript
export const Route = createFileRoute("/(fan)/profile")({
  loader: loadProfileRouteData,
  pendingComponent: ProfileSkeleton,  // ← required
  component: ProfileScreen,
});
```

## Every Async Mutation Must Show Pending State

Use `LoadingButton` with `loadingLabel`, or disable controls and show a spinner during mutations. Never let users submit twice.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<LoadingButton isLoading={isSaving} loadingLabel="Saving...">Save</LoadingButton>

// ❌ BAD — no pending feedback
<button onClick={handleSave}>Save</button>
```

## Background Refresh Failures Must Be Surfaced

No empty `.catch(() => {})`. At minimum, set an error flag that the UI can display. Use `retryWithBackoff` for automatic retries:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — retry + surface error
retryWithBackoff(() => fetchData(), { maxAttempts: 2 })
  .then(data => set({ data, error: null }))
  .catch(error => set({ error }));

// ❌ BAD — silent failure
fetchData().catch(() => {});
```

## Use `InlineErrorState` for Recoverable Errors

When an operation fails and the user can retry, use the existing `InlineErrorState` component with an `onRetry` callback:

```tsx
{error && (
  <InlineErrorState
    message={getUserMessage(error)}
    onRetry={() => refetch()}
  />
)}
```

## Upload Progress Must Reflect Reality

If the upload API does not support progress events, do not show a fake progress bar. Either implement real progress tracking (XHR `onprogress` or Supabase resumable uploads) or show an indeterminate spinner.

## Validate Media at Selection Time

Validate file size and type immediately when the user selects a file. Do not wait until upload to reject. Use `validateImageFile`, `validateCoverMediaFile`, or `validateGalleryFile` from `@/lib/utils/image-compress`.
